#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129283 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128861 :question/id #uuid "6102567f-7035-5fa2-b12e-80a0470de4a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12418" :question/problem "Sketch the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by \n$$\n\\mathbf{T}: \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \n\\longrightarrow \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u {e}^{v} \\\\ {u}^{2} - {v}^{2}\\end{array} \\right]},\n$$\nis (locally) orientation-reversing." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y)}{\\partial (u, v)}  <    0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}: \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u \\\\ v\\end{array} \\right]} \n\\longrightarrow \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}u {e}^{v} \\\\ {u}^{2} - {v}^{2}\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{v} & u{e}^{v} \\\\ 2u & -2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{v}\\cdot (-2v)-u{e}^{v}\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-2{e}^{v}({u}^{2}+v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{v}({u}^{2}+v) & <0 \\\\ {u}^{2}+v & >0 \\\\ v & >-{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-u^2\n$$\n\ndefines a downward-opening parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/2b/2b6128c5a1737e3ad1fd82f91f5ccd320421ad3472ae8152440034ecea10d364.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "091b8235-56d8-5a08-bc95-08c99772cfd8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050992 :topic/difficulty 1.1523219435529348 :topic/id #uuid "77b779f9-f0f6-53e5-821f-44c6d9f4ce47" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124636} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124637} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124638} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124640}] :topic/math-academy-id 1899 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048259} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049133} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049477} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050207} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050289} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050800}] :topic/title "The Domain of a Multivariable Function"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186730679 :question-generator/id #uuid "cbe40d2e-9f39-5d46-9c86-26720e15ad9d" :question-generator/script "generators/8e/8e31deade570f62df49c513e7538429747d8c381e27d943c7a52870f5e01e184/17592186129283.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "061056bc-bfce-5ff4-8595-a2d484ecafcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09f7f36ecc2197cc95e1878fa22ac22367978809a5241f09886a7eb2fab071f3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275531} {:answer/id #uuid "16f3a484-24df-5d26-8a99-6de6aa5fdb49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/15/154f70201a5a00737d8df61952f5600ff91a2373df07b0b54680fe84e048402c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275690} {:answer/id #uuid "5d63b3ec-601c-5feb-8242-cbcc9d6062a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276310} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb5eb91-0daf-521c-91f4-9877e03fe3e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276885} {:answer/id #uuid "ff869b8f-3276-5ccb-a221-37224323880c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "061056bc-bfce-5ff4-8595-a2d484ecafcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09f7f36ecc2197cc95e1878fa22ac22367978809a5241f09886a7eb2fab071f3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275531} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd317045-c8ee-5fc6-a8f1-218f77e90e7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278085}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5ab6f10-630f-5f61-bd52-33e1fa95452d" :question/math-academy-id "q-160341" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ u-v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & -4v \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-1)-(-4v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2u+4v & <0 \\\\ 4v & <2u \\\\ v & <\\frac{1}{2}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{2}u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/09/09f7f36ecc2197cc95e1878fa22ac22367978809a5241f09886a7eb2fab071f3.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e468aabf-e6e4-5599-81b1-17dc6d355954" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389030} {:answer/id #uuid "bdeedbec-6bdf-59e7-9b2b-b9d5e4e3ee50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389031} {:answer/id #uuid "a24ff250-c577-5a6e-8589-b7fa78f56034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389032} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf74745-74d7-5023-8d2f-494bd3a4b62a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/15/154f70201a5a00737d8df61952f5600ff91a2373df07b0b54680fe84e048402c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389033} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a52325-f624-5716-886a-b507033c0141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/090bab0ac1c6356010d83a6ad54c59b53b7dd12062fb5e331a936ce3f3a1b411.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a24ff250-c577-5a6e-8589-b7fa78f56034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389032} :answer-field/id #uuid "391991ce-c7bf-55cb-8662-29196fd230b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389029}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4471fd6f-9a7d-5e2e-b974-bcbd5ed1ceb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-160601" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-v \\\\ 4u-{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}-v \\\\ 4u-{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2v)-4\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4uv+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4uv+4 & >0 \\\\ -4uv & >-4 \\\\ uv & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the solution $v<\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u>0$ and $v>\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u<0.$\n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{u}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48838786-15c4-529e-9b61-9a4ae3631e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279238} {:answer/id #uuid "644450bf-23df-5be6-9017-bc23e84a13fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/8382e54c1f91ff0e07910c1250c046413814748d9e7ef8968984b7223b43afcc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279504} {:answer/id #uuid "71de0d63-b9fe-5bf9-98a3-3aa0f0728bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279627} {:answer/id #uuid "743bb53f-15e9-5c76-9499-48070c482fc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7f/7f214af0b5d71689ec7f21fff043e1779f1d3244c13fdbaf7b8df7f408d66298.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279641} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8384cd-3f08-52be-b19d-6807ce1004b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/14015cadab7d5dc8a9c33d0c1a57a44a79506bd01ba9b1cfe8ec1d280eb3fbb6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "644450bf-23df-5be6-9017-bc23e84a13fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/8382e54c1f91ff0e07910c1250c046413814748d9e7ef8968984b7223b43afcc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279504} :answer-field/id #uuid "158dba50-6c99-530b-a3b4-71c1f3ef60c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280870}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "613ff480-77bb-508e-adea-361b7545c613" :question/math-academy-id "q-161838" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ {u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+v \\\\ {u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2u & 2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (2v)-(2u)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2v-2u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v-2u & <0 \\\\ 2v & <2u \\\\ v & <u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/83/8382e54c1f91ff0e07910c1250c046413814748d9e7ef8968984b7223b43afcc.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e5ece0f-ace5-59e3-8bac-5e7030391f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278998} {:answer/id #uuid "56614d5f-f51d-520c-bd5a-2efe188329bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279385} {:answer/id #uuid "63c73c6f-8214-55ad-9f4a-739379cccb77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cb/cb5b22ff46569b231d122c2ed11bd412907f36271a033d86769435adf9fe48c7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279499} {:answer/id #uuid "90ce74d2-cefd-5461-a622-b31141a5968a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279883} {:answer/id #uuid "df833e78-3be8-5410-bdd9-e871a352bba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90ce74d2-cefd-5461-a622-b31141a5968a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279883} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfbed5de-5d8f-51b2-a9bc-07694301ed70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281224}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92a30208-5e48-56e6-a327-0e416b1fdedd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161842" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3{u}^{2} & -v \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3{u}^{2})\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)-(1)\\cdot (-v) \\\\  & =v-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v-{u}^{2} & <0 \\\\ v & <{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv={u}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042e4157-bfc2-5a27-a5f2-30fa623a1739" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278625} {:answer/id #uuid "194e22f8-8fb9-57e0-b1f3-883c6f1f3c27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278813} {:answer/id #uuid "78185cb7-fed8-5728-84d4-f9c34d0ceb1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9cd254ac65dedfa4c720b18afd4f5c3c7676b4f21170930f78e9adac276317ee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279663} {:answer/id #uuid "a94b4a1e-0ac2-5b32-aa1a-639dcba8fbfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280095} {:answer/id #uuid "e67d90ab-d605-56d8-af8e-7db9618ee656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "194e22f8-8fb9-57e0-b1f3-883c6f1f3c27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278813} :answer-field/id #uuid "c65b41f9-3939-501e-8345-1125734187f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281181}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "553ab218-87bf-5c6a-b2ae-3d3c054a906a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161843" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4u+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2v \\\\ -2u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1-(-2u)\\cdot (2v) \\\\  & =4+4uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4+4uv & >0 \\\\ 4uv & >-4 \\\\ uv & >-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the solution $v>-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u>0$ and $v<-\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u<0.$\n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-\\frac{1}{u}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,1)$ and $(-1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n  \n\n![](images/c5/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e3e495a-4d39-5ca6-b3be-a0813078a0db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278868} {:answer/id #uuid "a23d32b3-d4d4-5e82-8301-ae2d3c9a6002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/613e83ce5ad6154905ec9001ece078309e396561e251e85455ff261bb4cd61a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280033} {:answer/id #uuid "d5175981-dd9b-5a24-a6b2-37545e23ce11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9e/9ecab1b0f048e83b57d04a60c1cf20ee5ed0e61257577cf42c1a091976c04473.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280472} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9b7a18-0143-5fce-848a-c380d264cf20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7f/7fc8ce1e1eaa3eb4e4acbbc167bdc4a479591bea21d2acdeaf799bd99d6b1150.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280544} {:answer/id #uuid "f5be8a96-29fb-524c-92e1-8f2da938314c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a23d32b3-d4d4-5e82-8301-ae2d3c9a6002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/613e83ce5ad6154905ec9001ece078309e396561e251e85455ff261bb4cd61a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280033} :answer-field/id #uuid "262596a8-f5e0-5444-9e30-382a5a13609e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280900}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee68f9ff-69b4-5317-9406-24330023ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-161855" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{uv} \\\\ {u}^{2}+v\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{uv} \\\\ {u}^{2}+v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}v{e}^{uv} & u{e}^{uv} \\\\ 2u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =v{e}^{uv}\\cdot (1)-(2u)\\cdot u{e}^{uv} \\\\  & ={e}^{uv}(v-2{u}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{uv}(v-2{u}^{2}) & >0 \\\\ v-2{u}^{2} & >0 \\\\ v & >2{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=2{u}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(0,1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/61/613e83ce5ad6154905ec9001ece078309e396561e251e85455ff261bb4cd61a0.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d480733d-2bef-5e70-8bd1-b1ffc7f1c3fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/427cb4b8e6497f75aecfe809aa084b0bf6f4ad167f3a0838aa40b1a50d115e1d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383549} {:answer/id #uuid "c32a224b-bb0d-59ed-877d-57206e5e909b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383550} {:answer/id #uuid "ecaf9992-c899-5cf7-95ad-9660ca75dce5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383551} {:answer/id #uuid "153ff83b-ae84-5113-a031-ffd9105e29be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383552} {:answer/id #uuid "c24435eb-c7ff-5866-926c-e388c2da1faf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b764651dbc7999e7af13214685796b