.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{u}^{2}+v & >0 \\\\ v & >-2{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-2{u}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/8b/8b35fbafaf8d121bceef7a0763253df075fe4fe85eb3c992f95c59d05f986c67.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2407dcd5-06ff-568b-bb6d-b2494e2bd942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389197} {:answer/id #uuid "07712d2e-2b92-521c-b6ae-d43d00f464d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389198} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3ba601-6388-5b1c-ac01-5522063f4425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fd2a51ca3a1654c2e857018268bf251366472a2c5d7f90009d5ccfbf1b1edd9d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389199} {:answer/id #uuid "dc797ebb-78cb-5a5b-ac03-97f75fe59dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389200} {:answer/id #uuid "2201cc6c-a008-5122-982f-2699a2c582b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95bf5e059fda0fc1ba8423b35fffa57d9cae0cc2a2a7e40b0c2539b6a7ae7678.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2407dcd5-06ff-568b-bb6d-b2494e2bd942" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389197} :answer-field/id #uuid "644861a4-b1bb-5e40-b887-ad0f73e8386a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389196}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82d50c5e-c224-54bc-84fa-f5633f671803" :question/math-academy-id "q-161840" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 2v \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (2v) \\\\  & =2u+2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u+2v & <0 \\\\ 2v & <-2u \\\\ v & <-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(-1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44718c67-0ba1-524e-9c98-36d26b5e3a27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389204} {:answer/id #uuid "225446d3-d261-5650-bed9-eaacbb9f2ba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389205} {:answer/id #uuid "f7224ff9-23ce-5fb3-a58f-396aece4ce79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fd2a51ca3a1654c2e857018268bf251366472a2c5d7f90009d5ccfbf1b1edd9d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389206} {:answer/id #uuid "133f4c43-8534-5694-8789-da248d6d37e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389207} {:answer/id #uuid "83b86f4d-ddaa-5fd0-acc9-387f47e13895" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b764651dbc7999e7af13214685796b5045fab89f101bbc72bf413112df3c51f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "225446d3-d261-5650-bed9-eaacbb9f2ba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389205} :answer-field/id #uuid "10f005f2-f2a3-59bb-859f-a90699b333ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389203}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4aa2b6c-6ba5-59e1-9b2a-ad9aa14c6d6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161841" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ -uv\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ -uv\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ -v & -u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot (-u)-(-v)\\cdot {e}^{u+v} \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}(v-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u+v}(v-u) & >0 \\\\ v-u & >0 \\\\ v & >u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(2,3)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/8b/8bec16b8ed5083071e21761e6b2e649e136ce0662f7e5ab764161491094c0609.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72f242ce-c65f-5c89-b0bc-7d65d210918f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389211} {:answer/id #uuid "62f79a35-0524-561a-ba91-d11cf1227837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d944eb13437b86c0cf6ae4fa8bca09031ed0f2f85a9f20bcb0050a6de9f8ebb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389212} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa99b0c-e94e-5958-a986-2c13e020da52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389213} {:answer/id #uuid "acff9e64-428c-54e8-8971-9f328584d347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389214} {:answer/id #uuid "2b75873a-335e-5bb0-9312-2f0d35d3633e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7bc22ac4dfd2d7015952144ece63f91ecccef2a992649aece60dc8a70f1d018.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfa99b0c-e94e-5958-a986-2c13e020da52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389213} :answer-field/id #uuid "317c3736-80dd-5537-ba65-91575de09aa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389210}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e552dcc6-87b8-5585-84f4-2c455a9099f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161856" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}+2v \\\\ -2u-{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}+2v \\\\ -2u-{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2v)-(-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-4uv+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4uv+4 & <0 \\\\ -4uv & <-4 \\\\ uv & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the solution $v>\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u>0$ and $v<\\frac{1}{u}$ for $u<0.$\n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{u}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,2)$ and $(-1,-2)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n   \n\n![](images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37a87cd5-635f-5714-9ff7-1501eac8f8a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/05/05a85c27c33421d67a198ab65111a484967eb8bf1ec97d5881b0b50c0b26c8ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541355} {:answer/id #uuid "54d432d4-57f5-50e0-a07b-4e0b563624ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d6d817325324661cf7b0b3a73a89a8d63558bd90ae268c7598092d5a1354c49.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541360} {:answer/id #uuid "cff99e6c-e58d-55f1-933a-16641bf95e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f0/f06ac726fc0c602ad63a5ac830702dbb7bb01bc9516e8df4a3e83107d0afa1d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541400} {:answer/id #uuid "de50e907-c0e5-59ab-b887-7778a4dcb99f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e2/e2890e20881a7bc6c3f537f62305bbf4aa6b9b1de4264fb8139520c9940d0e92.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541409} {:answer/id #uuid "e2070a2a-7767-5ba0-b7cc-05836a7e3971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9b/9bef2a7540d3ae348165a601cffddcf32ddcfca7207bb31f14f9053438d39c28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54d432d4-57f5-50e0-a07b-4e0b563624ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d6d817325324661cf7b0b3a73a89a8d63558bd90ae268c7598092d5a1354c49.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541360} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5bba0f6-32b6-5eda-9fcf-43279157826a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541394}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08434fb0-6532-59e4-bcda-afba09f8c2fa" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u - 12 \\\\ 2 \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u - 12 \\\\ 2 \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 v + 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(4)\\cdot (4 v + 8)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=16 v + 32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 v + 32 &<0 \\\\ v < -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -2\n$$\n\ndefines a horizontal line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/0d/0d6d817325324661cf7b0b3a73a89a8d63558bd90ae268c7598092d5a1354c49.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57964daf-2acf-57ba-b59c-295b8fceed9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/35/3514dfa39dddf1327e2d355ecfdf0c1a54596772554c49749e6f88c4f63e1c69.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541362} {:answer/id #uuid "af133e12-6645-589a-9628-434ecbaaaed3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/94/94f8fc7f53d269b8f902460bc29938d1bee5e71e9f8a4024e6916c9729cfe942.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541386} {:answer/id #uuid "af401e3c-68a4-5187-8578-6c3bd89fcc82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a9/a9652984e1c261b065dca8d9ab1fae943b7f549c363201495fa2d86dace43964.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541387} {:answer/id #uuid "d35b5cc4-4666-5871-9f4b-3e03ebb0a54a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dd/ddaffc1b9c44fc6aa22caac176f1fdd6e171c31e1246d884d25101473977fa9c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541403} {:answer/id #uuid "eb243a42-c920-525c-addf-01d6c2661a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e7531367df6e086f961f6e4b39f382eebbb1d674f8708414059675fde5795be6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d35b5cc4-4666-5871-9f4b-3e03ebb0a54a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dd/ddaffc1b9c44fc6aa22caac176f1fdd6e171c31e1246d884d25101473977fa9c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541403} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d482458-3681-59a2-a3cf-fe291c09a159" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541370}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1669c7a6-5e4f-5ea0-88e1-7712fde23a58" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u - 3\\right)^{2} + 4 \\\\ - 3 u - \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2} + 9\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u - 3\\right)^{2} + 4 \\\\ - 3 u - \\left(v + 2\\right)^{2} + 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u - 6 & 2 \\\\ -3 & - 2 v - 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u - 6)\\cdot (- 2 v - 4)-(2)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &=- 4 u v - 8 u + 12 v + 30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 4 u v - 8 u + 12 v + 30 &<0 \\\\ \\left(u - 3\\right) \\left(v + 2\\right) > \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $v > -2 + \\frac{3}{2 \\left(u - 3\\right)}$ for $u>3$ and $v < -2 + \\frac{3}{2 \\left(u - 3\\right)}$ for $u<3.$ At $u=3,$ the Jacobian is positive, so this line is excluded from the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -2 + \\frac{3}{2 \\left(u - 3\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/dd/ddaffc1b9c44fc6aa22caac176f1fdd6e171c31e1246d884d25101473977fa9c.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222535a2-4caf-5d24-8c9b-b56cfc089a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d20afed479d7bf650adc8540ba6f28f9d21243d7017ab3fe0691f5603078575e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541351} {:answer/id #uuid "30f473e9-a3c2-590b-817d-9c1f196951a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/5358c811168ad9ce8e801e22415864f34b5d694fa50e69aa03c352b7d153cfd5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541353} {:answer/id #uuid "c2885d29-2182-5713-9c10-f79670914ca1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6d/6d3dd3fffbd04ef723ec8bb0701747d5d7f973a23d2ecfdf0437f8827a6e0cec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541392} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5a6394-0db1-54ff-8432-b11565760ab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6bc5057212ab1c347102f5c09aa4d21eb9bb0f6215ed7294be4b30c127e90deb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541398} {:answer/id #uuid "d29f05f9-483a-506e-af21-2a64161880a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6f/6f964fd6850041d6454091d0232b5fc4866e8