ally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v + \\left(u + 3\\right)^{2} + 1 \\\\ - 3 u - \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2} - 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & - 2 v - 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u + 6)\\cdot (- 2 v - 2)-(1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &=- 4 u v - 4 u - 12 v - 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 4 u v - 4 u - 12 v - 9 &>0 \\\\ \\left(u + 3\\right) \\left(v + 1\\right) < \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $v < -1 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}$ for $u>-3$ and $v > -1 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}$ for $u<-3.$ At $u=-3,$ the Jacobian is positive, so this line belongs to the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -1 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/a7/a77c173f49ff007692a1f040708adecbe65b7b035ce776faef93de1f8ce6019a.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "675f8f01-4c56-5d4a-a654-9bcd0db9ac05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/26/26c6b06e7265268f7bebf6168a8c78757540cf0293ff4dd4ad05b789eb9fd40a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541367} {:answer/id #uuid "b246f7e9-f68f-5fc1-8278-87edbd99b3dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8ce7c030f900131fc3657c23518899642a6c2a2d85cfc133e55e5d7e57b6a0ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541388} {:answer/id #uuid "b3edee41-d23a-5b9b-8654-4f05dc12f80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1f/1f9b6cdb376451952b34f064c5ed296c5f0fee6c1