 u + 48 &<0 \\\\ u < -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nu = -3\n$$\n\ndefines a vertical line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/c5/c55116b6c9a7a78b548eaef6002dc56584ddf8498adb550335b3bf27593fb7ea.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "724de8f7-79a1-5698-8f05-517251248be1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bc/bccf613be460b4765579cd916f63a6c216880214174583c134fc398a9a5f3809.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541371} {:answer/id #uuid "82acfdb9-c6e4-5a67-b65f-7ec1696341e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e5b61a928312936f111db2d8d3ae870bdb6c2cb0bb27a1ba12db333c0aa76cfa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541373} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa52ab2-258a-5799-8dea-abbb50d3ed55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/61eb7087a9aa310143a93f0dd0cf549196c66536baa0570bb3b7158b934e38ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541375} {:answer/id #uuid "909033da-49b3-56e3-8b2d-b060b00f0eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/55c4523390f0c74b41c7572e5160e3db9ef596061d1b8cd70bfd30a265de4161.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541376} {:answer/id #uuid "d92365d2-3a8f-5b47-8625-dbb8d48d1016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/23/23b757a918d46889aa0786289dad81b089876b521c1f52cb94aa8c306cea284c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fa52ab2-258a-5799-8dea-abbb50d3ed55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/61eb7087a9aa310143a93f0dd0cf549196c66536baa0570bb3b7158b934e38ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541375} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aff8968-d096-54f6-8a79-ed279c14f061" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541379}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59add0cf-4e80-54d4-b7e4-f8be9314c117" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} + 2 \\\\ - u - \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2} - 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2 v + \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} + 2 \\\\ - u - \\left(v + 1\\right)^{2} - 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & - 2 v - 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u + 2)\\cdot (- 2 v - 2)-(2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ &=- 4 u v - 4 u - 4 v - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 4 u v - 4 u - 4 v - 2 &>0 \\\\ \\left(u + 1\\right) \\left(v + 1\\right) < \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $v < -1 + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(u + 1\\right)}$ for $u>-1$ and $v > -1 + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(u + 1\\right)}$ for $u<-1.$ At $u=-1,$ the Jacobian is positive, so this line belongs to the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = -1 + \\frac{1}{2 \\left(u + 1\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/61/61eb7087a9aa310143a93f0dd0cf549196c66536baa0570bb3b7158b934e38ff.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f408a0-6e39-5b2c-9d7b-1e9430158db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d9/d9383071f1ee1de5f6a619559bebb5c2bc60f09e74655a476dc11981e26d8b93.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541358} {:answer/id #uuid "6759a9bf-0828-5f66-a722-fd710424a2b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/64/645c29d8beb5ddfe4c108002292a7fc13c6fc62dba4a6f616d2e4cbce3181278.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541366} {:answer/id #uuid "6cded118-0827-53b0-a109-b308dbdffd78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/44/44a052682a5fc6f18580bf3c3bea2835352972a195ebb4dbfda452c7163f538b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541369} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8c6549-87e1-5473-bf2f-c1b31ae4d655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1b/1bb0a60cf8676d84fb9ff02d4dc1ae0b429c6aa8ea3911e4846bd6b9470ca05c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541372} {:answer/id #uuid "adcebe86-8756-5934-805b-e2b9a4a06122" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5bc82f3c47998e71524755031882b38c2eee0f9f2f09871f6fdaab12e5ba3841.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6759a9bf-0828-5f66-a722-fd710424a2b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/64/645c29d8beb5ddfe4c108002292a7fc13c6fc62dba4a6f616d2e4cbce3181278.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541366} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbab2ee8-9f6e-5401-8a20-1f037631d0aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541397}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b68b81d-0d26-5a45-aadd-1f07bfe3d5e1" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u + 12 \\\\ 4 \\left(v - 3\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 u + 12 \\\\ 4 \\left(v - 3\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 v - 24\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(4)\\cdot (8 v - 24)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=32 v - 96.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}32 v - 96 &>0 \\\\ v > 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = 3\n$$\n\ndefines a horizontal line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/64/645c29d8beb5ddfe4c108002292a7fc13c6fc62dba4a6f616d2e4cbce3181278.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "370415d1-58c4-5284-bfae-31a0be8367d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/5389d4bb3047ce09fdd363b74f11656401529f5385409f693c18a1c20cac51ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541354} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4383ff-729c-5878-8348-4f2b0d1ad4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c66e6dd0389d46178372b1cc1730b323671e6a7ea7010a8dc400866b63561409.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541359} {:answer/id #uuid "dc32f06a-61d1-5319-9f88-b0c254c6a451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/44/44ca94fdc013bdefb282eb0b215303330a93bb537b0327ab94506e8ae85b7abc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541406} {:answer/id #uuid "dd00d785-a141-5c1c-ace3-4a535de31478" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d285c5d86c19c425685fdb1fd693d3fae982cdcb0e9893e02c63093069f5fad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541407} {:answer/id #uuid "e29b2f7f-6be3-54e1-a9ee-2b64caa0a35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/22/22640ca71707c942eb71626a7eac145b85b4817493daf26d46934d8ca3a3912f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "370415d1-58c4-5284-bfae-31a0be8367d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/5389d4bb3047ce09fdd363b74f11656401529f5385409f693c18a1c20cac51ec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541354} :answer-field/id #uuid "abe07359-7db1-564f-b31e-da90ea4077ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541384}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b62ef8fc-d595-570e-8f35-4ca0887f510b" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3 v + \\left(u + 3\\right)^{2} - 9 \\\\ - u - \\left(v - 3\\right)^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}3 v + \\left(u + 3\\right)^{2} - 9 \\\\ - u - \\left(v - 3\\right)^{2} - 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 u + 6 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6 - 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(2 u + 6)\\cdot (6 - 2 v)-(3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ &=- 4 u v + 12 u - 12 v + 39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 4 u v + 12 u - 12 v + 39 &>0 \\\\ \\left(u + 3\\right) \\left(v - 3\\right) < \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $v < 3 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}$ for $u>-3$ and $v > 3 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}$ for $u<-3.$ At $u=-3,$ the Jacobian is positive, so this line belongs to the required region.\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nv = 3 + \\frac{3}{4 \\left(u + 3\\right)}\n$$\n\ndefines a hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/53/5389d4bb3047ce09fdd363b74f11656401529f5385409f693c18a1c20cac51ec.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83322a87-b177-543d-952d-ded93c066948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/86/86e54346d92ea3eca01c395db65de785091767172a164b2322bf8210ec54fdde.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541374} {:answer/id #uuid "a68cf97b-4f70-5306-aada-e38f431e0da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f4/f4c844177f02716ee92191f1452593fdaa20dd90fe2be545a794b51dfe8c0285.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541381} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e8272f-59d1-5036-8d5d-caf412d74ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b99527183109e4b5f9e870ddd4f0e2738f2642b22038990272263926155e7256.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541382} {:answer/id #uuid "aafc87e3-d56f-5184-93b6-549bc04e975d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/49a73fc6db51b1ec1e25c47c80ff1bef122494ecb078bb1e6b120ae1341a84fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541383} {:answer/id #uuid "d08235b4-1a47-57de-83fe-b206067560d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d8/d847bbc443a2fa8ea5715c1a97b0b2c5784cba321564775c2f81a02d0d11e95b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9e8272f-59d1-5036-8d5d-caf412d74ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b99527183109e4b5f9e870ddd4f0e2738f2642b22038990272263926155e7256.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541382} :answer-field/id #uuid "18452602-07b3-5f0d-a30a-ee8bb7add6b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541349}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4fbb398-85ee-59ed-888e-83228cf28f5c" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} \\\\ 3 v + 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\left(u + 1\\right)^{2} \\\\ 3 v + 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}8 u + 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(8 u + 8)\\cdot (3)-(0)\\cdot (0) \\\\ &=24 u + 24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24 u + 24 &>0 \\\\ u > -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the equation\n\n$$\nu = -1\n$$\n\ndefines a vertical line.\n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/b9/b99527183109e4b5f9e870ddd4f0e2738f2642b22038990272263926155e7256.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1745867c-2de0-5adf-8859-b6656e21d47a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a14192698baa5f54314d4325bcbc3e9d488ec728b0beee1570921e0869259da3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541348} {:answer/id #uuid "5e99e166-ec0c-5b27-a479-5d9471f471ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/98/98455798ceac32138f9619758059d300b0065853da4fd4bd83af8daedc69848d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541365} {:answer/id #uuid "b90f54e8-d871-567f-b5dd-68883fc7cf68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/898fd878de4c411294f1949a767f28c2b5d8b2f8c4f9096b5f78835fd51c31f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541391}